  "body": "We support configuring the GC thresholds via the [`gc_thresholds`](https://github.com/matrix-org/synapse/blob/develop/docs/sample_config.yaml#L151-L153) config option, however the default can lead to a lot of GC churn on busier instances. This can easily lead to a) a CPU usage by GC of ~20% and b) multiple multi second GC pauses in quick succession.\r\n\r\nSince we manually run the GC we could add limits to ensure we don't run the GC e.g. gen 0 no more than once a second, gen 1 no more than once every 10s and gen 2 no more than once every 30s. This a) enforces that we don't repeatedly do gen2 really frequently and b) stops objects getting promoted to gen2 far too quickly.",
